Weekly Breach Investigation
Breach: Composer Token Leak — GitHub Actions Exposure
Analyst: Jamal Mahmoad
Date: 2026-05-14

1. Executive Summary

A flaw in Composer, the PHP dependency manager, caused GitHub authentication tokens to leak into publicly visible CI logs.
The issue appeared when GitHub rolled out a new token format in April 2026. Composer rejected these tokens and printed their full values into logs, exposing credentials across thousands of projects.
The vulnerability poses serious risks to PHP projects using GitHub Actions, especially automated workflows.

2. Attack Timeline

Apr 2026: GitHub introduces new token format with hyphen.

Apr 2026: Composer rejects tokens, exposing them in logs.

May 2026: Researchers at Socket.dev flag the issue.

May 2026: Packagist urges immediate Composer update.

May 2026: GitHub rolls back token format temporarily.

Exploitation Path:

Run Composer inside GitHub Actions workflow.

Token with new format rejected.

Full token value printed in CI logs.

Logs accessible to anyone with permissions.

Credentials potentially compromised.

3. MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
Credential Access: Unsecured Credentials (T1552)

Defense Evasion: Masquerading / Error Message Exposure (T1036)

Execution: Command and Scripting Interpreter (T1059)

Persistence: Abuse of Configuration Files (T1112)

4. Detection Opportunities
Log Sources:

GitHub Actions CI logs

Composer error outputs

Container runtime telemetry

Detection Rules:

Alert on Composer authentication failures.

Monitor logs for exposed token strings.

Flag abnormal use of GITHUB_TOKEN in workflows.

5. Recommended Mitigations
Update Composer: Upgrade to 2.9.8, 2.2.28 LTS, or 1.10.28.

Audit Logs: Review recent CI logs for exposed tokens.

Rotate Credentials: Treat any exposed token as compromised.

Workflow Hardening: Avoid printing sensitive values in error messages.

Analyst Notes
This incident highlights how small validation flaws can lead to massive credential exposure.
Even though GitHub rolled back the new format, leaked tokens remain a risk.
Teams must patch Composer immediately and audit logs before GitHub retries the rollout
